# Project Equinox — Cursor Rules
# Cross-Venue Prediction Market Aggregation & Routing
# These rules apply to every file in this project. Never violate them.

## Project Identity
- Project Name: Project Equinox
- Language: Go 1.22+
- Purpose: Infrastructure prototype that connects to Kalshi and Polymarket,
  normalizes market data into a canonical internal representation, detects
  equivalent markets across venues, and simulates routing decisions for
  hypothetical trades.
- This is NOT a trading product. No real money, no real orders, no wallets.

## Core Architecture — Never Violate Layer Separation
The system has exactly these layers in this order:
1. Venue Connectors (venues/kalshi, venues/polymarket)
2. Normalizer / Adapters (venues/kalshi/adapter.go, venues/polymarket/adapter.go)
3. Canonical Models (models/)
4. Equivalence Detector (equivalence/)
5. AI Tool Layer (ai/, equivalence/tools/)
6. Routing Engine (routing/)
7. HTTP Server (server/)
8. Static UI (static/)

### Layer Rules — Strictly Enforced
- routing/ must NEVER import venues/ packages. It only sees canonical models.
- equivalence/ must NEVER make routing decisions.
- ai/ must NEVER call Kalshi or Polymarket APIs directly.
- server/ must NEVER contain business logic. Handlers call services only.
- normalizer/adapters must NEVER call external APIs. They only transform data.
- Heuristic layer must ALWAYS run before AI layer. AI is fallback only.

